  "question": {
    "text": "For the octahedral complexes of  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  in  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  (thiocyanato -S) and in  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  ligand environments, the difference between the spin-only magnetic moments in Bohr magnetons (when approximated to the nearest integer) is<br/><br/>[Atomic number of Fe = 26]",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "4",
  "solution": {
    "text": "As  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  and  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  are weak and strong ligands respectively so during complex formation their behaviours are different.<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  being a weak ligand can not pair inner 3d electrons so<br/><br/> <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  i.e.  <math><msub><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>18</mn></mrow></msub><mn>3</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> <br/><br/>For weak ligand,  <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo></math>  i.e. n = 5<br/><br/>As  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math>  being a strong ligand can pair inner 3d electrons so<br/><br/>For strong ligand,  <math><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msup></math> , i.e. n = 1<br/><br/>Magnetic moment  <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math> <br/><br/> <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>5</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math>  for weak ligand.<br/><br/>Magnetic moment for strong ligand  <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></msqrt><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>.</mo></math> <br/><br/>Difference in magnetic moment  <math><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>35</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>",
